# This fixture's value is that it is BYTE-IDENTICAL to `keld create hello`
# output at the pinned Keld SHA. `keld create` writes LF.
#
# keld-benches has core.autocrlf=true and no repo-level .gitattributes, so
# without this file a Windows checkout rewrites these files to CRLF and they
# stop matching `keld create` byte-for-byte — the blob stays LF but the
# working tree does not. That is not hypothetical: macos/keld/hello/index.html
# checks out at 366 bytes on Windows against its own 349-byte LF blob.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to the blob on every platform, so the
# byte-identity claim in FIXTURE.md is verifiable by anyone who clones,
# not only by whoever happened to author the fixture.
* text eol=lf
